cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "contextburn: a run-efficiency meter for language-model coding agents"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arsentev
    given-names: Evgenii
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9120-7298"
    website: "https://arsentev.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arsentev-ai/contextburn"
url: "https://arsentev.ai"
abstract: >-
  contextburn reads the local transcripts an LLM coding agent already writes and reports where the
  tokens actually went — by session, by machine and by reason. Beyond the usual counters it
  reports run efficiency: the share of paid tokens that became model output rather than a
  re-reading of context already sent. The share is given twice, by tokens and weighted by
  price, because the first is a property of agents and the second is a property of how the
  operator works. Nothing leaves the machine; the tool makes no network calls.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - coding agents
  - context window
  - token accounting
  - observability
  - cost efficiency
license: MIT
